.TH IMUD\-MAVLINK 8 "July 2026" "imud 1.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-mavlink \- bridge imud's binary stream to MAVLink over UDP/serial
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-mavlink
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-mavlink
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and emits MAVLink for ArduPilot, PX4, or a ground station (QGroundControl,
Mission Planner).  It sends
.B HEARTBEAT
(#0) at 1 Hz and, at
.IR rate_hz ,
.B ATTITUDE
(#30) and/or
.B ATTITUDE_QUATERNION
(#31).  MAVLink protocol version 1 or 2 is selectable.
.PP
The bridge is pure C (a hand-rolled encoder, no external dependencies).  MAVLink's
body frame is FRD/NED \(em the same as imud \(em so roll/pitch/yaw, the gyro body
rates, and the quaternion pass through directly (SI radians / rad/s).  It reads the
stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled, and it reconnects automatically if imud restarts.
.PP
Output goes to
.B UDP
and/or
.B serial
simultaneously (each independently enabled).  Serial is opened raw, 8N1, at the
configured baud; the shipped unit grants the service the
.B dialout
group and tty-device access.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Load configuration from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf .
Only the
.B [imud-mavlink]
section is read.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The protocol version, rate, message selection, UDP
destination, and log level are applied live; the system/component ids and which
transports are enabled require a restart.  If the reload fails to parse, the
running configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Read from
.I /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
(the
.B [imud-mavlink]
section); the keys are documented in
.BR imud-mavlink.conf (5).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run against a local ground station on UDP:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-mavlink --config /etc/imud/imud-mavlink.conf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and
.B enabled
in
.IR imud-mavlink.conf ):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-mavlink
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud-mavlink.conf (5),
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud-signalk (8),
.BR imud-mqtt (8),
.BR imud-influxdb (8),
.BR imud.conf (5)
